{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>and who, the rest of my people</b> — the righteous." "<b>They broke open</b> — they called, as in: \"they broke forth in song\" (Isaiah 54:1). And some say: they broke and divided, as in: \"deal your bread to the hungry\" (Isaiah 58:7), the shin in place of the samekh, and the meaning is: they broke." "<b>the pot</b> — like a cooking-pot or like a bowl."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The two prooftexts cited are Isaiah 54:1 and 58:7; chapter numbers not given in the Hebrew, resolved by the verse content."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:49.689092588Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}